(o/'README.md').write_text("# Individual and class-group firing ranges — 2026-09-15\n\nOwner approved individuals and class groups after accepting the original individual look. This extension adds faint soft outlines for each selected member of one weapon class. There is no group fill. Overlap uses a maximum mask in one shader pass, so crossing or coincident outlines cannot add opacity. Each unit retains its equipped weapon model/tier range. The individual shader is byte-identical to the accepted version.\n\nManual same-class selections (Shift/card/box) also qualify. Mixed-class selections and Select All suppress all range graphics. Select All has explicit display-only controller metadata, so even a homogeneous full squad remains clear; choosing its class explicitly shows the outlines. A group reduced to one living selected unit returns to individual presentation. Clear selection, battle exit, hidden view and invalid equipment remove stale graphics. No combat/order behavior, HUD dimensions, camera, audio or portraits changed.\n\nRuntime scope: new gameplay/tactical_group_range.gdshader; group support in tactical_selection_range.gd; five display-metadata insertions in tactical_orders_controller.gd. The earlier eight-line tactical_battle_view.gd layer wiring is retained unchanged. A group uses one cached bounds quad and maximum-alpha shader; the shader bounds32 entries, above current legal squad sizes. Do not infer a larger gameplay cap from this internal capacity. Single and group quads are reused, with only one visible at once.\n\nValidation: official Windows Godot4.7.2 native, 1440x1000. group_validation.json contains164 checks across Harold/bridge/estate, all five real class buttons, each member's actual range, class/single/mixed/All transitions, manually selected pairs, full12-unit homogeneous selections, movement/zoom, death reduction and unchanged paused combat state. Five actual rendered-pixel checks include twelve coincident outlines exactly matching one, crossing masks matching max rather than summed alpha, transparent interior/outside and visible alpha capped near0.105. Existing individual native suite234 rerun separately; both reports/logs are saved here. Total398 checks, zero final failures/script errors. Fifteen native group screenshots; Harold pistol, bridge rifle and estate pistol visually inspected. No broad FPS/whole-battle regression campaign or owner acceptance of the group appearance is claimed.\n\nInitial test-fixture issues: first click arrived before active HUD settled; add300ms settle. Homogeneous test changed class without changing model IDs, so canonical profile validation correctly rejected invalid equipment; fixture now equips valid Glock17 models and restores original pairs afterward. No runtime change was needed for these corrections. fixture_correction_groups.log and fixture_correction_group_validation.json preserve the failed equipment-fixture results.\n\nReproduce: run.py starts separate native windows with the normal official Godot console binary, first res://tools/selected_range_groups_20260915/check_groups.gd, then res://tools/selected_range_20260915/check_native.gd. No live-source pack rebuild or user sandbox termination. Reopen the normal sandbox to load changes. Baseline snapshots/hash receipts and final source hashes preserve current mixed working-tree ownership.\n\nRecords: journal selected-range-05 authorization, -06 validation checkpoint, -07 final result; Tactical Controls rules, Project Control and Hive Mind. Preview: libfile_dc8a5348e68c8191a128d8afca8c77f5. Existing publication block from selected-range-03 remains; no commit/push attempted in this extension. The old individual-only publisher/hash manifest is intentionally stale and must be replaced with the complete validated group scope if explicit publication approval arrives. Next: owner uses the class selectors and reviews the appearance.\n",encoding='utf-8')
